WEBVTT

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.870
To what end? Why create such an elaborate plan?

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.330
You're a man who seeks mysteries.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.830
As such, the answer is a matter of course.

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:58.830
You want to know who it is that can create
the ultimate mystery, don't you?

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:04.330
So, shoot me! Do that, and you'll--

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.950
<i>The mist is hiding the sin</i>

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.700
<i>I hold in my hand the LIST of judgment</i>

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.330
<i>I'm gonna do the perfect crime</i>
<i>and bury them in a cist</i>

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:54.580
<i>That's my DYING WISH for you</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:01:54.580 --> 00:02:00.040
<i>Guys of the privileged class torment the weak</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.120
<i>And they enjoy it</i>

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:08.660
<i>That's a bloody world, an endlessly</i>
<i>discriminatory society (dystopia)</i>

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:13.660
<i>Happiness does not bloom here</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:16.790
<i>We are oppressed</i>

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:22.370
<i>We must do something. Come on</i>

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:28.830
<i>Let the end begin</i>

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:34.660
<i>Break it to relieve your soul</i>

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:40.620
<i>Open your eyes. You'll be reborn</i>
<i>when you lose your life</i>

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:45.700
<i>We're lords of crime. We're sacrifice for ideals</i>

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:57.950
<i>Freedom lives forever, even if we die</i>

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.950
"The Two Detectives Act 1"

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:17.330
Thanks to the papers splashing the news
that Sherlock had caught Drebber's true killer,

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:22.000
his renown as a detective leapt to prominence.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:28.160
Ever since, we have had many visitors
here at 221B Baker Street,

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:33.450
and Sherlock has solved each case they
brought to him, one after another.

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:38.370
However, whilst his fame
as a detective has risen,

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:43.660
I have found him looking glum and
brooding more and more frequently.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.580
This is so dreary.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:56.450
How did things end up this way?

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:01.080
The riddles that you seek
keep coming to you nonstop.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.040
I should think you have nothing
to complain about.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:07.620
These sorts of banal mysteries
are not what I seek!

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:10.290
Banal?

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:14.250
I want to solve a much bigger mystery.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.620
The one who left my name at a crime scene

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:21.750
and dared me to solve the
mystery of Drebber's murder--

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:26.910
The mastermind whom the true killer,
Hope, referred to as his benefactor.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:32.700
I want to reveal who that is
and what objective they hold.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.750
Sherlock...

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.620
Leave me to myself for a while.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.330
All right.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:52.910
I have heard stories about your
exploits, Inspector Lestrade.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:56.620
Oh! Please remain still!

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:27.000
During the case on the <i>Noahtic</i>,
there was a mastermind who set up Enders.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:34.500
And Drebber's killer, Hope, had someone
who carefully planned out the crime for him.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:06.540
Sherlock Holmes...

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:09.790
I've heard about you.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:15.870
Would you care to make a deal with me?

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:23.200
If you accept my proposal,
I'll let you in on a secret.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:26.290
About the one who plotted out
Drebber's murder from start to finish,

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:32.950
and even directed me as to how
to pull it off--my benefactor.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:46.660
My benefactor holds you in high esteem.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:52.790
Enough to leave your name at the scene--
to see if you can solve the case.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:59.750
Yes, indeed. My benefactor truly is amazing.

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:05.000
When I arrived at Drebber's
mansion at the appointed time,

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:11.160
the door opened as if by magic,
and there was not a soul around to interfere.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.540
A true criminal genius.

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:20.660
Someone like that wanted to test me.
But to what end, exactly?

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:37.500
What if...? What if, at that moment...?

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:59.120
Yeah... What if, at that moment, I...?

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.500
John, what's happening?!

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:22.040
I don't know! Suddenly I heard gunfire!

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:23.540
Sherlock!

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:32.750
Was that your doing just now?

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.540
What was that?! Is everyone all right?!

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:41.410
Oh, Sherlock was just...

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:46.580
Holmes, were you the one who was shooting?

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:49.580
Yeah, to get you to come up here.

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:57.620
I know that when you're off-duty at this hour,
you're getting a trim from the nearby barber.

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.540
Then just come and get me like a normal person!

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:01.910
Lestrade...

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:06.450
Tell me if there have been any cases recently
where aristocrats have died.

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:09.790
Aristocrats? Why do you ask?

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:12.700
Just tell me! Have there been any, or not?

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:18.330
Now that I no longer have a line on this fellow,

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:22.540
I have no choice but to grasp at
any possibility, no matter how slim.

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:24.200
Now that you mention it,

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:28.200
I heard that the Viscount of Redshire
passed away on a lakefront in York.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.370
Tell me everything.

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:36.450
As I recall, he wrote a note saying
he was going for a walk late at night,

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:39.750
then proceeded to collapse
at the nearby lakefront.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:42.540
He had a chronic illness and there
was nothing criminal in nature,

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:45.250
so his death was attributed to his illness.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:48.580
Now that I've told you,
what do you intend to do?

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:50.450
We're going to go there and investigate.

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:52.830
Investigate? Investigate what?

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:56.540
Isn't that obvious? Whether or
not his death was a murder.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.830
Wh-What?!

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:58.750
For Heaven's sake, when you said you wanted
to re-examine Lord Redshire's death,

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:01.700
I half-suspected that there were
some new facts about the case.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:03.160
Is this it?

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:15.910
When the viscount left his mansion for his walk
that evening, where was his body later found?

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:21.700
Let's see, as I recall, it was at
the base of a conspicuous oak tree.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:30.660
It has been several days
since the body was found.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:33.370
I rather suspect there aren't
any clues left to be found.

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:35.700
Mind your own business and keep quiet!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:48.620
The train bound for London will be leaving
from Platform 3 momentarily!

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:52.790
All passengers, please board
as quickly as possible!

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:56.120
Damn, I came all the way to York for this.

00:11:56.120 --> 00:12:00.790
He really did die of his illness,
and this was all for naught!

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:04.620
Holmes, it looks like you bet
on the wrong horse this time--

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:09.910
I-I'm going to go buy a newspaper.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.250
I'll come have a drink with you
in the restaurant car later.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:15.830
Very well, we'll see you then.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:19.750
Honestly, to hell with your death by illness.
Get yourself killed, seriously.

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:22.450
Sherlock, you're acting like a child.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:26.830
You have to stop acting so frustrated
just because things didn't go your way.

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:28.870
Damn, I'm out of matches.

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:30.910
John, match.

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:34.870
You smoke too much. Doing everything
to excess is bad for your health.

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:36.580
You should quit, already.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:39.790
Leave it alone and just give me one!
I know you have some!

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:43.540
How can you speak to me like that?!
Don't you know how to ask nicely?!

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:47.160
Huh?! You are useless, you know that?!

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.790
Useless, am I?

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:53.620
You know, you're partly to blame for me
being so upset in the first place!

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.450
How do you figure that?!

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:58.450
Why did you stop me when you did?

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:02.540
When I did what? Do you mean
when we had Hope cornered?

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:04.040
Yeah, that's right!

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:09.040
Are you saying that if I hadn't stopped you,
you would have shot him?

00:13:10.790 --> 00:13:14.910
I should have shot him when I could. If I had...

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:16.830
Sherlock!

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:19.290
It's what he wanted, too!

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:24.080
If I had killed him back there, I would have
been one step closer to a huge mystery!

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:28.620
I am profoundly disappointed in you.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:31.580
I had no idea you were such
a worthless scoundrel.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.910
Huh?

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:36.950
If you wish to become a murderer,
do it without me.

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:40.500
Go ahead and pursue your beloved mysteries,
or whatever else you like.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.160
But do it alone.

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:50.580
What's the matter with him?

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:55.580
All aboard for London!
The train is departing shortly!

00:13:57.620 --> 00:13:59.000
Tch.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:21.790
It's locked?

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:35.410
Tch. Fine, then. I suppose I'll go eat.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:45.700
Here you are, sir.

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:47.160
Yeah.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:52.120
Confound that John. What is he, a woman?

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.450
He can't be serious.

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:01.540
Sorry, but I'm changing tables!

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.500
S-Sir?

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:12.580
Yo, Professor.

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:16.370
Fancy meeting you here.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:30.290
Yo, Professor.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:33.620
Fancy meeting you here.

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:36.040
Sherlock Holmes!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.290
What is he doing here?

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:44.870
You're that man with whom I sailed
together on the <i>Noahtic</i>...

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.250
Sherlock.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:52.700
I read about you in the newspaper.
You solved the case of Count Drebber's murder.

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:55.120
I'm at my wit's end about that.

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:58.660
I intended to have Lestrade
take all the credit for it,

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:03.370
but either somebody leaked it,
or a reporter sniffed it out.

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:05.120
I do not see the problem.

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:09.870
As a result, your fame as a detective has risen,
and you've gained more clients, have you not?

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:12.160
Hmm, well, yeah.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:16.660
But I have no interest in those dull,
tuppenny-ha'penny cases.

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:17.910
What interests me is--

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:23.290
Mr Holmes, begging your pardon,
but we were just finishing our meal.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:26.700
You haven't even been served
your dessert or digestif, right?

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:28.120
Why, you...

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:30.410
Just let me bend your ear for a bit.

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:35.500
I do not mind. We were just starting
to grow bored, as well.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:39.160
As it happens, I went to York
to investigate a case,

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:42.080
but it turned out to be not
at all what I thought it was.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:44.250
Well, that is a pity.

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:45.540
Isn't it though?

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:51.290
I thought it was another in a series
of cases involving noblemen.

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:53.750
A series?

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:55.660
Yeah.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:17:00.910
I think there are some commonalities
between two of these cases.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:03.950
Enders and Drebber were both aristocrats,

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:08.580
and following both their cases,
their misdeeds in life came to light,

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:11.290
and their scandalous conduct
was trumpeted about.

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:13.790
But there was one other thing.

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:18.700
In both cases, there was a mastermind
behind the scenes, pulling the strings.

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:23.290
Your first common point does not
strike me as being very distinctive.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:27.290
It also concerns me that you have
but a mere two parameters.

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:34.410
Moreover, isn't the presence of this mastermind
nothing more than your own presumption?

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:39.870
I daresay you're right. But as testament
to there being a mastermind,

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:44.040
there was a proposal made to me
by this individual behind the scenes,

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:47.000
extended via Jefferson Hope.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:50.910
If I killed Hope, they would
tell me who they were.

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:53.540
That is quite the odd bargain.

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:59.330
Isn't it? But I did not accept it,
nor did I kill Hope.

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:01.450
A very wise decision.

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:07.080
However, after Hope was taken
into custody, I went to visit him,

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:09.580
where he secretly told me something--

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:15.330
the name of the mastermind who
provided him his murderous scheme.

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:25.000
You were his benefactor, weren't you...

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:29.200
...William James Moriarty?

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:40.000
Is this a bluff?

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.290
It would be simple for Holmes
to find out about Brother

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:46.250
from the information he received
aboard the <i>Noahtic</i>.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:52.080
After all, there cannot be many young
college mathematics professors

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:54.660
who are also sons of aristocrats.

00:18:54.660 --> 00:19:00.250
Also, following his incarceration,
we kept watch over Hope's surroundings,

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:03.700
and he had no contact with
anyone from the outside.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:11.040
Meaning that we know that Hope had no
opportunity to reveal Brother's name to Holmes.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:15.330
But if Brother denies
Holmes's bluff based on that,

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:19.330
it will acknowledge that we
were involved in the incident.

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:25.660
Holmes, you rascal. I should eliminate you
before you are beyond our control.

00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:29.580
Indeed...

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:32.330
...that is a most amusing assertion.

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:37.120
However, it is impossible to prove
that I did not do something.

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:44.500
Also... it would be <i>your </i>job to prove
that I did it, would it not?

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:53.950
I'm kidding! I'm kidding! That would be
a case of <i>probatio diabolica</i>, after all!

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:56.000
Sorry, sorry!

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:59.250
Still...

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:04.830
I was just thinking how great it would be
if you were the sharp-witted mastermind.

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:16.950
"Catch me if you can, Mr Holmes"...

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:28.000
Would it satisfy you to hear
me say that, Mr Detective?

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.750
You really are the best!

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:37.040
I see that my joke was well received.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.660
Oh, you and I are seriously
going to get along famously!

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:42.500
Holmes...

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:44.620
Oh, here you are.

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:47.540
Holmes, who are these gentlemen?

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:52.870
The Moriarty family's second son, William,
and his adoptive younger brother, Louis,

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:54.910
am I right?

00:20:54.910 --> 00:20:57.700
Just how much does he know about us?

00:20:57.700 --> 00:21:03.290
Please excuse my interruption.
Lestrade of Scotland Yard, at your service.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:06.660
You are? I have heard so much about you--

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:15.200
What is it?!

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:19.450
I-I heard a loud sound from the
neighbouring compartment moments ago,

00:21:19.450 --> 00:21:22.450
and when I came to see what the matter was...

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:30.790
It's locked!

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:33.160
H-Hey, Holmes!

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:37.160
Yeah, he's dead. Have a look.

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:40.200
It's clearly a murder.

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:41.790
Murder?!

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:49.660
So, Liam, you have nothing to do
before we reach London, do you?

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:52.830
Shall we have a contest to see
who can find the culprit first?

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:56.660
Wh-What are you talking about?!
This is a murder case, not a game!

00:21:56.660 --> 00:22:00.700
Very well. That might be interesting.

00:22:00.700 --> 00:22:04.580
However, the case appears
to be a bit more complicated.

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:05.870
Huh?

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:20.290
<i>An oath committed by souls assumed,</i>

00:22:20.290 --> 00:22:24.500
<i>with ideals that wallow in genetic karma</i>

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:43.580
<i>Lie! Be resolute if you're going</i>
<i>to share your pain</i>

00:22:43.580 --> 00:22:45.830
<i>(Demonstrate your resolve)</i>

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:49.370
<i>Like, dislike, you can't afford</i>
<i>to care either way</i>

00:22:49.370 --> 00:22:52.580
<i>It depends on the objective</i>
<i>(Making it happen is what's most important)</i>

00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:56.080
<i>The necessary evil of self-sacrifice</i>

00:22:56.080 --> 00:22:59.700
<i>is a righteous cause that no one can comprehend</i>

00:22:59.700 --> 00:23:03.450
<i>Take pride in the inviolable bonds shared</i>

00:23:03.450 --> 00:23:08.290
<i>among brothers who bear the same crime</i>

00:23:08.290 --> 00:23:11.950
<i>Make a chance trigger your inevitable stance</i>

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:13.620
<i>and get drunk on your accomplishments</i>

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.410
<i>at the end</i>

00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:18.580
<i>Don't believe in what you can see,</i>

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:22.830
<i>in truths there's no point in knowing</i>
<i>(Whatever it takes)</i>

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:29.450
<i>Defer to its own validity,</i>
<i>you only have one goal</i>

00:23:29.450 --> 00:23:30.950
<i>(Let me hear you say)</i>

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:37.790
<i>You can't lie to yourself, come along with me</i>

00:23:40.700 --> 00:23:43.410
<i>It's all because there is no answer</i>

00:23:43.410 --> 00:23:45.790
